<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia May housing finance falls 8.4 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia May housing finance falls 8.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia fell 8.4 percent by volume to 39,933 dwellings in May from an April level of 43,598, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance fell to A$4.24 billion in May from A$4.62 billion in April, the bureau said.</p>
<p>Analysts forecasts had centred on a fall of 5.7 percent in volume commitments for May.</p>
</text>
